dates postgresql_functions v1
description "Two dates whose aliases share their first 63 bytes. PostgreSQL keeps 63 bytes of a name, and the two functions take the same types, so the second replaces the first and answers for both (W001). Every other target takes them as they are"

inputs
  received : date  range >=2026-01-01 <=2026-01-31

date the_day_an_order_placed_during_the_spring_campaign_of_2026_ships_by_post = received
  + 3 days

date the_day_an_order_placed_during_the_spring_campaign_of_2026_ships_by_courier = received
  + 1 day
